    61	## 4. [x] DONE 2026-08-28 — Wire the gatekeeper's merge into the flow (the door has no doorbell)
    62	`harness/gatekeeper.py::merge` is complete and tested (including against a real git repo)
    63	but NOTHING calls it — no route in `harness/server.py`, no tool in `harness/chief.py`, no
    64	step after the panel certifies a job. `dispatch.ship` is gone, so today nothing can move a
    65	job to `shipped`. Task: after `gauntlet.run_panel` certifies a job (`result.certified`),
    66	ask the gatekeeper to merge — through `gatekeeper.handle({"verb":"merge", ...})`, never by
    67	importing `merge` directly into the worker (the point is that agents ASK). Note the ship
    68	guard also needs a passing cross-family TESTER on the record (schema guard 6), so for now
    69	a certified job without a tester verdict will be refused — log that refusal plainly on the
    70	job, don't work around it. Tests: certified job + tester → shipped; certified job, no
    71	tester → refused with a plain-English note, job stays `done`. Do NOT weaken any guard.
    72	
    73	## 5. [x] DONE 2026-08-27 (Connection: close on refusals) — Gatekeeper HTTP surface: drain the body on early refusals
    74	`harness/gatekeeper.py` `serve()`: the 403 and 413 paths return without reading the
    75	request body, so on a keep-alive connection the leftover bytes are parsed as the next
    76	request line. Read and discard `Content-Length` bytes (bounded) or send
    77	`Connection: close` before returning. Add a test with a raw socket. No other changes.
    78	
    79	## 6. [x] DONE 2026-08-28 — Merge holds a write transaction across `git merge`
    80	`gatekeeper.merge` runs `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` → `set_status` → `git merge` (up to 120s) →
    81	`COMMIT`, while `connect()` sets a 15s busy timeout — so a slow merge turns concurrent
    82	panel writers into "couldn't finish" skips. Either raise the busy timeout above the merge
    83	timeout in `harness/db/jobs.py::connect`, or restructure so git runs outside the
    84	transaction against a re-checked precondition. Say which and why in the worklog.
    85	
