   138	## 11. [ ] Pin the tester's evidence to the version (schema, deliberate)
   139	`guard_tester_must_cite_artifacts` (schema.sql ~829) matches artifacts on job_id only.
   140	A screenshot captured for version A would satisfy a tester verdict on version B. Add a
   141	`reviewed_version` (or `head_version` snapshot) column on artifacts, stamped at capture,
   142	and make the guard require `a.reviewed_version IS NEW.reviewed_version`. Numbered
   143	migration + schema.sql in step; `test_live_db_matches_schema` must pass after applying.
   144	Design with Sol first (it's a guard change).
   145	
   146	## 12. [ ] Merge-time bundle contract, a commit-time size limit, and pushing job/N
   147	`gatekeeper.merge` recomputes `git merge-base main tip` at merge time and compares
   148	that FRESH computation against the stored bundle — which means the base it
   149	verifies against can differ from the base the panel actually reviewed against if
   150	`main` moved in between (task #9's design review flagged this: the check can be
   151	correct today and still verify against the wrong thing tomorrow). Store the FULL
   152	base commit id (not just the diff text) and the exact `git diff` options used
   153	(`--no-renames`, pinned) at build time, and make `gatekeeper.merge` verify against
   154	THAT STORED BASE, never a recomputed one — if `main` has moved, that's a new
   155	integration and needs a fresh review, not a silent re-verify. Separately:
   156	`_claude_cli_build`/`_commit_diff_in_clone` have no upper bound on how large a
   157	change they'll accept before committing — a commit-time size limit (mirroring
   158	gauntlet.py's MAX_CODE_CHARS truncation-avoidance design for reviews) belongs here
   159	too, refused BEFORE a commit exists rather than truncated after. And today nothing
   160	ever pushes `job/<id>` anywhere — when auto-merge is eventually enabled (after the
   161	real OS isolation boundary Sol's design gate is still waiting on), the
   162	gatekeeper's merge needs to push the merged `main` to the real remote, behind the
   163	same lock, with the same "refuse and say so" discipline as every other step in
   164	that function. Design each of these with Sol before building, same as task #9
   165	itself was.
   166	
   167	## 13. [ ] Run builders and reviewers as the `chiefagent` account (the wall, harness side)
   168	BLOCKED until the owner creates a standard (non-admin) macOS user `chiefagent` and signs
   169	in to Claude Code + Codex as that user once. Then, in this order, each with a live check:
   170	1. Keys: `~/.chief/env` stays owned by the owner, mode 600. Builders/reviewers receive NO
   171	   vendor keys. The xai reviewer runs in the harness process (owner), not as the agent.
   172	2. Layout: `/Users/chiefagent/work/job-<id>/` owned by chiefagent for clones; the record
   173	   (`harness/db/chief.db`), the real repos and `~/.chief` unreadable to chiefagent
   174	   (`chmod 700` on the owner's home is the simplest — verify Jess/Chief repos too).
