   218	    `HARNESS.parent` (this repo) regardless of which repo actually owned the
   219	    worktree, which leaves a stale entry behind in the project's REAL repo forever
   220	    (git worktree metadata lives with the repo that created it, not the worktree
   221	    directory itself — removing the directory from the wrong repo's cwd does
   222	    nothing to that repo's own bookkeeping). `conn` is what lets this resolve which
   223	    repo that is; every caller already has one.
   224	    """
   225	    dest = WORKTREES / f"job-{job_id}"

codex
The current record guards are strong against inconsistent rows, but weak against a lying reporter. For example, the record verifies that a reported reviewer seat is configured as a higher-tier family; it does not verify that the named reviewer ran. Likewise, it rejects an artifact labeled “model,” but accepts the same bytes if the caller labels them “harness.” Moving those writes behind a network API without changing provenance would turn several hard gates into self-certification.
